      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To find \\(\\det(\\mathbf{M}^4)\\) given that \\(\\det(\\mathbf{M}) = -2\\), we can use the property of determinants for matrix powers. Specifically, the determinant of a matrix raised to a power is the determinant of the matrix raised to that power, i.e., \\(\\det(\\mathbf{M}^n) = (\\det(\\mathbf{M}))^n\\).\n\nGiven:\n\\[\n\\det(\\mathbf{M}) = -2\n\\]\nwe need to find \\(\\det(\\mathbf{M}^4)\\).\n\nUsing the property of determinants, we have:\n\\[\n\\det(\\mathbf{M}^4) = (\\det(\\mathbf{M}))^4\n\\]\nSubstituting the given value of \\(\\det(\\mathbf{M})\\):\n\\[\n\\det(\\mathbf{M}^4) = (-2)^4\n\\]\nCalculating \\((-2)^4\\):\n\\[\n(-2)^4 = (-2) \\times (-2) \\times (-2) \\times (-2) = 16\n\\]\nTherefore, the value of \\(\\det(\\mathbf{M}^4)\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{16}\n\\]",
