      "text": "To find \\(\\det (\\mathbf{M}^4)\\) given that \\(\\det (\\mathbf{M}) = -2\\), we can use a property of determinants. Specifically, for any square matrix \\(\\mathbf{M}\\) and any positive integer \\(n\\), the determinant of \\(\\mathbf{M}^n\\) is given by \\(\\det (\\mathbf{M}^n) = (\\det (\\mathbf{M}))^n\\).\n\nGiven:\n\\[\n\\det (\\mathbf{M}) = -2\n\\]\n\nWe need to find \\(\\det (\\mathbf{M}^4)\\). Using the property mentioned above:\n\\[\n\\det (\\mathbf{M}^4) = (\\det (\\mathbf{M}))^4\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the given value:\n\\[\n\\det (\\mathbf{M}^4) = (-2)^4\n\\]\n\nCalculating \\((-2)^4\\):\n\\[\n(-2)^4 = 16\n\\]\n\nThus, the determinant of \\(\\mathbf{M}^4\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{16}\n\\]",
